# Payroll API deployment environment. Copy to deploy/.env, replace
# every CHANGE_ME value, then check it before the first start:
#
#   cp deploy/.env.example deploy/.env
#   node deploy/check-env.mjs --target compose --file deploy/.env
#
# This file holds placeholders only and check-env refuses it as is.
# Never commit deploy/.env (it is in deploy/.gitignore).
#
# Passwords: at least 24 characters from A-Z a-z 0-9 _ - only (they go
# into connection URLs), one different value per role. Generate each:
#   openssl rand -hex 24

# --- Read by docker-compose.yml -------------------------------------

# Superuser of the PostgreSQL container. Used only by the image's first
# start to create the database and run deploy/init-roles.sql, and by an
# operator for restores. The API never sees it.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_postgres_superuser

# payroll_owner: owns the database and the tables, runs migrations.
# Given to the one-shot migrate job only.
PAYROLL_OWNER_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_owner

# payroll_runtime: the API's login. No superuser, no BYPASSRLS, owns no
# table; may only SET ROLE payroll_app.
PAYROLL_RUNTIME_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_runtime

# payroll_backup: read-only (pg_read_all_data plus BYPASSRLS) for
# pg_dump and the audit chain check. Keep it off the API container.
PAYROLL_BACKUP_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_backup

# 32 random bytes, base64. Wraps every company's data key: sealed salary
# and bank fields and TOTP secrets cannot be read without it. Back it up
# apart from the database backups. Generate once:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Losing it loses the sealed data. Changing it breaks every sealed
# field (there is no rotation yet; see docs/ops/runbook.md).
PAYROLL_MASTER_KEY=CHANGE_ME_base64_32_bytes

# Host port the API is published on (the container listens on 8787).
# Put a TLS reverse proxy in front; do not expose this port publicly.
API_PORT=8787

# Optional. Tag for the locally built image (default: local).
# PAYROLL_API_TAG=local
# Optional. Base image for the build (default: node:22-bookworm-slim).
# NODE_IMAGE=node:22-bookworm-slim

# --- Read by the API itself (compose builds these from the above) ---
#
# Set these directly only when running the API without compose
# (`pnpm api:dev`, a platform service, Kubernetes, and so on).
#
# DATABASE_URL          runtime role, for example
#   postgres://payroll_runtime:<password>@<host>:5432/payroll
# MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL  owner role (migrations). If unset the API uses
#   DATABASE_URL, which fails with the roles above: always set it.
# PAYROLL_MASTER_KEY    as above.
# PORT                  listen port, default 8787.
# RECEIPTS_DIR          required: absolute directory for encrypted
#   receipt files (compose uses the `receipts` volume). Back it up
#   with the database: a restored database without it lists receipts
#   whose files are gone.
# Optional channel providers (Plan 13; each is "not configured" until
#   its group is complete; the list is in HANDOVER.md): POSTMARK_*,
#   EMAIL_FROM, WHATSAPP_*, INBOUND_EMAIL_*, GOOGLE_OIDC_*, ENTRA_*,
#   PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL, PUBLIC_APP_BASE_URL (https).
# VERIFY_DATABASE_URL   backup role, for deploy/verify-audit-chain.ts.
#
# Check them with: node deploy/check-env.mjs --target api
